In my current game, I tamed a large cat and brought him down a few
levels to where I'd found a polymorph trap.  I pushed him onto it, and
he turned into a lichen.  No good.  Several pushes later, the lichen
became an ettin mummy.  Better, but I kept at it, and soon I had a pet
arch-lich!  For only the second or third time ever, in my personal
experience.  I cackled with glee and immediately took him on a
shopkeeper-slaying tour of the dungeon.

Later, Richie Lich (as I christened him) saved me from a huge hassle.
He was next to me as I was about to step through a doorway, and I got
the message "Wait! There's something there you can't see!" followed by
"Something sucks Richie Lich's brains!"  D'oh, invisible mind flayer!
Conveniently forewarned, I beat a hasty retreat, put on a blindfold,
and took out the nuisance with missiles.  Only later did it occur to
me how strange that must have looked from my character's perspective:
undead brain-dust suddenly and mysteriously vacating the lich's
various skull-holes.

I'm a little curious about what happened when my lich took on an
aligned priest: absolutely nothing.  He "touched" the priest, with
absolutely no effect, as a stethoscope examination showed.  But
usually when a lich touches a monster, the monster is "covered in
frost," perhaps without effect if the monster is cold-resistance.  But
there's no message at all for lich vs. priest.  What's up with that?


